A||||55||WKDFIRO||Stupid Things People Told You About Your Fiero||||8||
Z||000000||WKDFIRO||01-24-2000||08:39 PM||||Nothing amuses me more when people who never owned a Fiero, never driven a Fiero try to act like an expert on the Fiero to me. "Oh those are junk cars they all catch fire..." etc. The first car I bought with my own money was an 87 4 cylinder, I have an 85 GT now and my wife has her own 87 4 cyl.<P>I am writing what I think will be a hilarious article for my club asking the question, What was the most stupid thing somebody told you about your Fiero?<P>I would love to hear your responses and we can ALL have a good laugh! Thank you very much for your input!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Richard Parnell||01-24-2000||08:51 PM||||The usual stupid remarks are what I've heard, <BR>It's not safe. (This from a riceburner owner who's car dented when I leaned against the fender).<BR>It catches on fire you know, (this from a guy with a rag stuffed into his gas tank filler opening, really!).<BR>They're hard to work on, (have you tried to work on ANY new car lately?)<BR>I'm sure there are more and I'll send them as I remember them.<BR>||||reg||12
