Z||000019||fierospeeder||01-25-2000||08:16 PM||||My friend says sell my 87 tbird turbo coupe 2.3l and keep my fiero.  I have three cars.  Going to keep all of them anyhow.  <BR>The fiero has less problems. says my friend.<P>Maybe thats why all the used fieros have oxidized paint, the previous owners never waxed them. <P>Coworkers say isn't that car unsafe, but they always ask wheres it at because they want to see it again.<P>Number one for me is probably that its the most unsafest car.  <BR>People saying its hard to fix is a joke, because the 2.5l engine has been around for a long time.  <P>My opinion, the car is easy to fix.  Not to complicated then my tbird.  The 2.8 is the same, my moms wagon has the same engine.<P>Doesn't the car breakdown a lot?  I see a lot of newer cars on the side of the road.<P>The cars start on fire.  I drove my 2.5 84' without a belt 2 miles till i reached a trak auto, overheating.  The car runs fine after me driving it without a belt, maybe because i keep the oil level wheres its suppose to be.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||fierosound||01-25-2000||08:20 PM||||Funny thing about people - you would think they'd apply that same "helpful" reasoning and advice when talking about most 6 figure exotics...<P>- so low - your a** is on the ground<BR>- so small - dangerous if hit by a truck<BR>- fibreglass - it's not strong so it's dangerous<BR>- hard to get parts<BR>- hard to work on  and so on...<P>But exotics are cars that (probably) neither they, their relatives or friends will never own.  They therefore cast aside all objections and say "great car".  Even if you did get one, for some reason they don't feel the need to be "helpful" and point out it's (in THEIR opinion) "shortcomings". <P>A Fiero is a mid-engine sportscar within their reach.  Many have to convince THEMSELVES why they shouldn't follow your lead - and they have to do this by "remembering" every flaw (real or imagined) that they ever heard or read about on the Fiero.  Often they have their facts wrong anyway!<P>Get a motorcycle - you'll get the same attitude.   Why can't people mind their own business,  especially on subjects they are totally ignorant about???  Sheesh!!!<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000021||fiero56||01-25-2000||09:49 PM||||I'm always hearing "dont hit anything, the gas tank is in the middle". My response is remember the chevy truck gas tank placement problems. Whenever I don't take the Fiero to work, I am constantly being asked "where is the Fiero", and "I'm going out to lunch, can I take the Fiero". These are the same people who remind me how unsafe my car is. Go Figure. <BR>Off topic- Fierospeeder reminded me of a Drew Carry episode. Drew is about to bite into a cheeseburger at the bar, and a guy at a neigboring table exclames "don't eat that, it'll give you a heart attack!" Drew comments on how people should mind themselves and shut up. I guess you had to se it.||||reg||1
