Z||000051||stimpy||02-05-2000||07:54 PM||||veering away from the stupid things people say to exhaust tips (hey, why not?) pretty much any tip you can think of can work, just get your local muffler shupto weld them on.  I have 2 flat oval Megs tips on my gt. They fill the cut outs very well and mimic the shape of the tips on newer Pontiacs...Grand Prix,etc. I also think that the tips on the latest Cadillac Sevilles look mighty mighty fresh, but I bet they would be mighty mighty $$$$.  ||||reg||1
Z||000052||fierosound||02-13-2000||05:10 PM||||This forum started about stupid things people told you about your Fiero...<P>One of the biggest things you get negative comments about is the plastic body, which in fact is one of the best things about a Fiero IMO.  They seem to think is so unique, that it was an "experiment" that didn't work out.<P>To these people I point out the other plastic vehicles GM made:<P>Buick Reatta 2 seat sportscar<BR>Chev Lumina APV van<BR>Pontiac Transport van<BR>Olsmobile Silohette van<BR>Saturn<BR>Corvette<P>The Saturn is heavily advertised as having rust/dent resistant polymer panels.  And of course, the Corvette, also had a body not of metal, but fiberglass.  GM sold alot of these "non-metal" bodied cars...<P><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000053||Oreif||02-13-2000||10:51 PM||||Just so everyone knows one of the reasons GM stopped making the Fiero was to make the plastic vans. There were 3 machines used for the plastic panels. 2 were used for the vans the 3rd was taken by the original Fiero management. Who by the way started Saturn! Then when GM stopped making the vans out of the plastic, Saturn scooped them up and now you have the LS series. So in a round about way Saturn's are the 2nd generation cousin to the Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000054||Raydar||02-14-2000||11:37 AM||||"Fiero? That's that 'gay little two-seater' that doesn't have any power." (From one of my wife's friend's teenage sons. What a little dip$hit.)||||reg||1
